      "description": "Watch Slavia Praha SLA vs Lens highlights and goals from UEFA Champions League on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on September 10, 2026. Slavia Prague and Lens faced off in a high-stakes UEFA Champions League encounter on September 10, 2026, under the bright lights of a packed stadium. Both teams entered the match with high ambitions, looking to secure a vital result in one of Europe’s most prestigious competitions. A Tense Beginning and a Sudden Turn The first half was a cautious affair, with both sides testing each other without finding a breakthrough. However, the game exploded into life early in the second half. In the 49th minute, Slavia Prague suffered a major setback when Mikulas Konecny was shown a straight red card for pushing an opponent. Despite being down to ten men, the home side shocked the visitors just two minutes later. Danijel Sturm picked up the ball outside the box and unleashed a left-footed strike that flew into the net, giving Slavia Prague a 1-0 lead. Lens Push Back and Late Chaos Lens responded by ramping up the pressure, utilizing their numerical advantage. Their persistence paid off in the 73rd minute when Odsonne Edouard set up Abdallah Sima , who slotted home the equalizer. The drama intensified as the clock ticked toward the 90-minute mark. In the 88th minute, Danijel Sturm appeared to have won it for the hosts, scoring his second goal of the night with a powerful right-footed shot from distance to make it 2-1. The Stoppage-Time Miracle The match was far from over. As five minutes of stoppage time were announced, Lens launched a desperate final assault. In the 91st minute, Mezian Soares delivered a perfect cross for Florian Thauvin , who headed home to level the scores at 2-2. With Slavia Prague reeling, Lens struck the final blow in the 93rd minute. Ruben Aguilar found space outside the area and struck a low right-footed shot into the corner, completing an incredible comeback and securing a 3-2 victory in a night that will be remembered for its sheer unpredictability."
